# Feature: drop zone (Phase 9)

Library screen `#dropzone`: drop WAV files or folders. Renderer uses `pathForFile` + `statPath`. Only directories and `.wav`/`.wave` files are sent to Python.

`classify_and_ingest {paths}` moves tagged originals into `libraryRoot`. First analyze can be slow (YAMNet load). Disable further drops while `ingesting`.

`#ingest-jobs` lists per-file status from progress events (`inspect` → `analyze` → `tag` → `move` → `done`/`error`) and the final job results (`→ Pour` or error text). Then `list_library` refresh.

Prevent window default drag/drop so Chromium does not navigate. Python still walks folders for WAV; non-WAV inside a folder is skipped by ingest expand.
